# Docker stack refresh after edits

When you change anything under **`apps/api/`**, **`apps/web/`**, **`infra/docker/`**, Dockerfiles, **`package.json`** scripts that affect the compose build, or **`pnpm-lock.yaml`** / **`requirements.txt`** used in images:

1. From the **repository root**, run **`pnpm docker:up:detached`** (full rebuild + recreate + start in background).
2. Do **not** consider the task complete until that command finishes successfully (exit code 0).
3. If only one tier changed, you may use the narrower scripts instead: **`pnpm docker:rebuild:api`** (api + worker) or **`pnpm docker:rebuild:web`** (web only).

If Docker is unavailable in the environment, say so explicitly instead of silently skipping.
